From 77f772a1cf18f77d527a8163ba32c862a4a04eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0xFFshell <0xffshell@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:57:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: count the keys' write surface

Every rule this fork has about walking is a rule about the key stream - KeyBeat's beat
between a direction and its opposite, HeadFirst's hold while the head comes round,
CarefulFooting's stance across a movement seam, SprintWindup, atAPace - and all of it
reaches the game through PlayerMovementInput#tick, out of InputOverrideHandler. That is
worth exactly as much as the number of places that go around it, and nothing in the suite
said how many that is.

The fifth count, after CameraWritesTest, HandWritesTest, ButtonWritesTest and
ClickGatesTest: the files that may write the player's own movement input, the lines those
files have to keep so the list cannot go stale, and the two places the key state is read
(the LookBehavior read, and the sprint redirect in MixinClientPlayerEntity, which answers
vanilla's own sprint question and is where the sprint doctrine can otherwise be lost
without a test seeing it).

Teeth checked by mutation in a scratch tree, all three reverted byte-identical: a sprint
forced outside the handler in MineProcess fails the count; removing
'sprintNextTick = shouldSprintNextTick();' fails the shapes; removing the flag write
itself fails the count from the other side. HUMANLIKE.md's test list now names it.
---
 HUMANLIKE.md                                  |   7 +-
 .../java/baritone/utils/KeyWritesTest.java    | 242 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 247 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/test/java/baritone/utils/KeyWritesTest.java

